
Steps to extract the data and provide in csv or json format to an individual from kibana

For a one-off request where you need to extract Elasticsearch data and provide it to an individual, I’d use Discover for CSV and Discover/Dev Tools for JSON, depending on volume.

Option 1 — Export CSV from Kibana Discover
Go to Kibana → Discover.

Select the correct Data View / index.

Set an absolute time range, for example:
01-Aug-2026 00:00 → 31-Aug-2026 23:59

Apply the required KQL filters, for example:

monitor.name : "Application-A"
Add only the fields the individual actually needs, for example:

@timestamp
host.name
source.ip
event.action
message
Validate the records and record count.

Preferably Save the Discover session so the exact query, filters, columns and sorting are retained.

Select Export → CSV / Generate CSV.

When generation completes, download the CSV from the notification or Stack Management → Reporting.
